1
00:00:28,800 --> 00:00:32,299
"My Rival and Me"

2
00:00:32,300 --> 00:00:34,300
(Episode 5)

3
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:46,320
Aren't these offerings a little strange?

4
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:51,150
[Guanyin, the Goddess of Mercy,
grants all requests for children.]

5
00:00:53,240 --> 00:00:56,159
Is it really appropriate for us to pray
here?

6
00:00:56,759 --> 00:00:58,000
Well, we're here already.

7
00:00:58,079 --> 00:01:00,280
It's the New Year. Everyone's got it
tough.

8
00:01:01,000 --> 00:01:02,000
Ah.

9
00:01:02,280 --> 00:01:04,000
The three great Chinese virtues.

10
00:01:24,000 --> 00:01:28,938
Goddess Guanyin, please bless Lan
Jue, the drama Gu Yiliang and I are in.

11
00:01:29,126 --> 00:01:34,404
We've poured so much into this
production. It's like our own child.

12
00:01:34,429 --> 00:01:38,596
Please let filming go
smoothly and make it a hit.

13
00:01:47,480 --> 00:01:49,319
What did you wish for?

14
00:01:49,640 --> 00:01:50,840
I wished that tomorrow's lunch

15
00:01:51,000 --> 00:01:52,599
won't have twice-cooked pork again.

16
00:01:54,439 --> 00:01:55,560
That's all you wished for?

17
00:01:55,760 --> 00:01:56,760
When you make a wish,

18
00:01:56,959 --> 00:01:58,959
you wish for whatever matters most right
now.

19
00:01:59,159 --> 00:02:01,239
I've had that dish four days in a row.

20
00:02:01,519 --> 00:02:02,319
If I keep eating it,

21
00:02:02,439 --> 00:02:04,040
my tongue will be twice-cooked too.

22
00:02:04,719 --> 00:02:06,040
What about you?

23
00:02:06,120 --> 00:02:07,120
What did you wish for?

24
00:02:10,080 --> 00:02:11,439
It won't come true if I tell you.

25
00:02:17,120 --> 00:02:20,479
Oh, that smile. I love it.

26
00:02:29,560 --> 00:02:31,560
Oh, right. You still haven't told me

27
00:02:31,759 --> 00:02:33,759
why you thought I was unhappy.

28
00:02:34,759 --> 00:02:36,840
It's... nothing.

29
00:02:38,039 --> 00:02:39,960
I remember you saying you're a theory guy.

30
00:02:40,080 --> 00:02:42,599
Acting takes observation of real life.

31
00:02:43,039 --> 00:02:44,758
Without life experience,

32
00:02:44,759 --> 00:02:46,759
your acting will seem very unnatural.

33
00:02:50,319 --> 00:02:51,679
Why bring that up all of a sudden?

34
00:02:52,280 --> 00:02:54,280
Because you've been acting unnatural all
day.

35
00:02:54,360 --> 00:02:56,056
It wasn't until I saw you smile at the
temple

36
00:02:56,080 --> 00:02:57,319
that you seemed like yourself.

37
00:02:58,039 --> 00:02:59,199
I have good reason to suspect

38
00:02:59,400 --> 00:03:01,479
you've been studying something behind my
back.

39
00:03:05,000 --> 00:03:06,960
You haven't been reading novels, have you?

40
00:03:11,520 --> 00:03:13,400
I don't know why you're reading them,

41
00:03:13,719 --> 00:03:15,199
but you don't have to copy anyone.

42
00:03:15,759 --> 00:03:17,039
You're already great as you are.

43
00:03:17,919 --> 00:03:18,599
Let's go.

44
00:03:18,800 --> 00:03:20,080
We still have lines to rehearse.

45
00:03:57,280 --> 00:03:58,599
Looks like

46
00:03:58,680 --> 00:04:00,800
I need a whole new kind of sugar-daddy
arrangement

47
00:04:00,879 --> 00:04:03,280
to protect him properly.

48
00:04:03,360 --> 00:04:04,360
Mm.

49
00:04:05,159 --> 00:04:07,280
A healthy sugar-daddy model for the new
century.

50
00:04:08,280 --> 00:04:11,360
We need moral, intellectual and physical
growth.

51
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:13,080
Mm.

52
00:04:23,279 --> 00:04:24,319
Mr. Gu?

53
00:04:24,879 --> 00:04:25,879
What brings you here?

54
00:04:32,560 --> 00:04:33,959
This... is for you.

55
00:04:34,439 --> 00:04:35,679
Take a look when you have time.

56
00:04:39,269 --> 00:04:40,429
[Self-improvement for Actors]

57
00:04:41,879 --> 00:04:43,199
Instead of sleeping at this hour,

58
00:04:43,480 --> 00:04:45,319
he's worrying that I'm too uncultured?

59
00:04:47,000 --> 00:04:48,480
I don't care about dignity.

60
00:04:48,879 --> 00:04:50,279
I don't care about pride.

61
00:04:51,120 --> 00:04:52,279
All I want is you.

62
00:04:53,040 --> 00:04:55,160
We may start out with nothing,

63
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:56,199
but

64
00:04:56,360 --> 00:04:57,560
I believe in you.

65
00:04:58,399 --> 00:05:00,120
We'll always be together.

66
00:05:00,839 --> 00:05:01,839
You.

67
00:05:03,120 --> 00:05:04,120
Only you.

68
00:05:06,839 --> 00:05:08,838
Oh, my dear friend.

69
00:05:08,839 --> 00:05:10,720
Oh, my esteemed boss.

70
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:12,800
Reviewing your past performances

71
00:05:12,879 --> 00:05:14,680
is another way to learn.

72
00:05:15,279 --> 00:05:18,160
Your earlier acting was a little stiff,
though.

73
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:19,480
Stiff?

74
00:05:21,160 --> 00:05:22,879
Forced.

75
00:05:23,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Forced?

76
00:05:25,720 --> 00:05:26,720
Unpolished.

77
00:05:26,800 --> 00:05:27,800
Unpolished?

78
00:05:29,839 --> 00:05:31,879
Mr. Gu, please stop trying to comfort me.

79
00:05:32,120 --> 00:05:34,800
I know exactly how good I am.

80
00:05:35,120 --> 00:05:37,279
Please... spare me.

81
00:05:38,079 --> 00:05:39,079
It's all right.

82
00:05:39,680 --> 00:05:41,480
Let's watch your earlier work.

83
00:05:43,439 --> 00:05:44,560
Back when I was a student,

84
00:05:44,759 --> 00:05:46,959
I thought the law protected people too.

85
00:05:47,720 --> 00:05:48,319
Huh?

86
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:51,279
I think Zhang sent the wrong edit.

87
00:05:51,480 --> 00:05:52,360
Never mind that.

88
00:05:52,439 --> 00:05:53,560
I've seen this drama.

89
00:05:54,920 --> 00:05:56,240
Once I entered the real world,

90
00:05:56,399 --> 00:05:57,480
I realized

91
00:05:58,600 --> 00:06:00,120
it was all fucking bullshit.

92
00:06:00,560 --> 00:06:02,360
The law only protects the rich.

93
00:06:03,000 --> 00:06:04,040
The truly poor

94
00:06:04,680 --> 00:06:06,759
can't even afford a copy of the
Constitution.

95
00:06:08,240 --> 00:06:09,240
Your Honor,

96
00:06:10,399 --> 00:06:12,359
how do you expect the old, weak, sick and
disabled

97
00:06:12,680 --> 00:06:15,079
to get back the money that's rightfully
theirs?

98
00:06:16,480 --> 00:06:17,878
At the heart of this character

99
00:06:17,879 --> 00:06:20,839
is a young man's idealism shattered by
reality.

100
00:06:20,959 --> 00:06:23,720
He can't be truly good, but he's not
entirely bad either.

101
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,198
So when you played him,

102
00:06:26,199 --> 00:06:28,600
you didn't explode or break down.

103
00:06:28,839 --> 00:06:30,399
You made it a confession instead,

104
00:06:30,480 --> 00:06:32,319
letting the audience feel his remorse.

105
00:06:32,439 --> 00:06:33,439
Am I right?

106
00:06:34,879 --> 00:06:35,879
Yes.

107
00:06:35,920 --> 00:06:38,719
This is a classic clip in the Niangzi
fans' tragic edits.

108
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:40,920
I know it inside out.

109
00:06:44,920 --> 00:06:46,040
Hey, Mr. Gu.

110
00:06:46,160 --> 00:06:47,415
Where are you going? Aren't we studying?

111
00:06:47,439 --> 00:06:49,160
No... no need. You're very good.

112
00:06:49,199 --> 00:06:50,199
Hey, Gu...

113
00:06:53,720 --> 00:06:56,120
Why the hell are you blushing?

114
00:07:03,399 --> 00:07:05,720
An all-night shoot, and now tennis after
wrap?

115
00:07:06,560 --> 00:07:08,480
What an energetic day.

116
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:10,199
Filming keeps us working nonstop.

117
00:07:10,319 --> 00:07:12,319
A little exercise helps relieve stress.

118
00:07:13,639 --> 00:07:14,639
Fancy a game?

119
00:07:14,720 --> 00:07:15,759
You're on.

120
00:07:27,439 --> 00:07:28,480
I'm warning you,

121
00:07:28,879 --> 00:07:31,399
I'm a man destined to be the Prince of
Tennis.

122
00:07:32,160 --> 00:07:33,360
That good, huh?

123
00:07:33,680 --> 00:07:35,079
I'd better watch out, then.

124
00:07:36,540 --> 00:07:40,120
At this distance, I should
be able to resist him, right?

125
00:07:46,040 --> 00:07:48,399
You can't return my serve.

126
00:07:59,319 --> 00:08:01,519
Damn it! I wasn't ready!

127
00:08:01,560 --> 00:08:03,519
That wasn't my real serve.

128
00:08:06,759 --> 00:08:09,399
This is my real serve.

129
00:08:20,920 --> 00:08:22,079
This side feels awkward.

130
00:08:22,279 --> 00:08:23,279
Let's switch sides.

131
00:08:25,000 --> 00:08:26,000
Okay.

132
00:08:44,960 --> 00:08:46,360
Just you wait, Gu Yiliang.

133
00:08:55,879 --> 00:08:58,440
Gu Yiliang, I'll battle you till dawn!

134
00:09:02,240 --> 00:09:03,240
Again!

135
00:09:04,440 --> 00:09:07,320
No more. No more.

136
00:09:07,519 --> 00:09:10,039
I need... a ventilator.

137
00:09:13,679 --> 00:09:14,679
All right.

138
00:09:24,480 --> 00:09:26,120
Yes! I won! I won!

139
00:09:26,200 --> 00:09:28,360
I won! I won!

140
00:09:28,440 --> 00:09:30,120
Gu Yiliang, I won!

141
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:31,200
Yeah!

142
00:09:36,700 --> 00:09:39,132
So distance has nothing to do with it.

143
00:09:42,025 --> 00:09:43,025
That's a wrap!

144
00:09:45,440 --> 00:09:47,399
I'm exhausted.

145
00:09:48,320 --> 00:09:49,320
Oh, Lucas.

146
00:09:49,600 --> 00:09:51,080
Tomorrow's call sheet is out.

147
00:09:51,120 --> 00:09:52,456
We need the early morning light for some
shots,

148
00:09:52,480 --> 00:09:53,760
so please come early for makeup.

149
00:09:53,840 --> 00:09:54,320
Okay.

150
00:09:54,399 --> 00:09:55,816
I'll stay at the crew's hotel tonight.

151
00:09:55,840 --> 00:09:56,639
I definitely won't be late.

152
00:09:56,759 --> 00:09:57,320
Great.

153
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:58,655
It's already late. Get some rest.

154
00:09:58,679 --> 00:09:59,679
Okay.

155
00:10:07,879 --> 00:10:09,919
You're done filming, right?

156
00:10:10,080 --> 00:10:11,279
It's late.

157
00:10:11,960 --> 00:10:13,320
What can I do for you, Mr. Cheng?

158
00:10:14,519 --> 00:10:16,559
When are you coming home?

159
00:10:16,759 --> 00:10:17,855
I'm not coming back tonight.

160
00:10:17,879 --> 00:10:18,639
Tomorrow morning...

161
00:10:18,640 --> 00:10:20,080
I'm not feeling well.

162
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,559
Not feeling well?

163
00:10:23,600 --> 00:10:24,919
Why don't you see a doctor?

164
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:26,639
I only want to see you.

165
00:10:31,759 --> 00:10:32,440
Okay.

166
00:10:32,639 --> 00:10:33,639
I'll be right there.

167
00:10:44,080 --> 00:10:45,080
Cheng Yan?

168
00:10:46,399 --> 00:10:47,399
Cheng Yan?

169
00:10:51,639 --> 00:10:53,120
Where are you?

170
00:11:16,120 --> 00:11:17,120
What are you doing?

171
00:11:18,039 --> 00:11:19,840
Isn't this why you called me back?

172
00:11:20,279 --> 00:11:21,279
The contract says

173
00:11:21,440 --> 00:11:22,879
I have to come whenever you call.

174
00:11:23,039 --> 00:11:25,440
Next time, don't bother pretending to be
sick.

175
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,200
Do you regret it?

176
00:11:29,080 --> 00:11:30,080
No.

177
00:11:30,440 --> 00:11:31,480
I chose this.

178
00:11:33,799 --> 00:11:34,799
Let's get on with it.

179
00:11:35,320 --> 00:11:37,120
I still have to get back to the set
afterward.

180
00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:40,200
You can go.

181
00:11:42,399 --> 00:11:43,399
What do you mean?

182
00:11:43,879 --> 00:11:45,159
Are you fucking messing with me?

183
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,240
Yes.

184
00:11:47,399 --> 00:11:48,399
I'm messing with you.

185
00:11:48,759 --> 00:11:50,200
It's your fault for falling for it.

186
00:11:55,480 --> 00:11:56,639
You're sick.

187
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:43,600
Here, have some water.

188
00:12:44,639 --> 00:12:46,399
You worked hard just now.

189
00:12:46,519 --> 00:12:47,600
Have some of this.

190
00:12:52,440 --> 00:12:53,639
It's all right, Zhu Mingming.

191
00:12:54,600 --> 00:12:56,200
So what if I had to fall into the water?

192
00:12:56,639 --> 00:12:58,119
So what if I don't have an assistant?

193
00:12:58,519 --> 00:13:00,200
As long as I can keep playing this role,

194
00:13:00,639 --> 00:13:01,639
that's good enough.

195
00:13:02,240 --> 00:13:03,240
Keep going.

196
00:13:09,759 --> 00:13:10,759
Here.

197
00:13:17,879 --> 00:13:18,879
Lucas.

198
00:13:19,039 --> 00:13:19,879
I just heard

199
00:13:20,000 --> 00:13:21,639
your real name is Zhu Mingming, right?

200
00:13:22,840 --> 00:13:24,280
Can I call you Mingming from now on?

201
00:13:24,440 --> 00:13:25,120
Sure.

202
00:13:25,240 --> 00:13:26,655
Remember to take a shower when you get
back,

203
00:13:26,679 --> 00:13:28,320
and change into clean clothes.

204
00:13:28,840 --> 00:13:29,279
Okay.

205
00:13:29,320 --> 00:13:29,759
I'm off.

206
00:13:29,799 --> 00:13:30,799
Thank you.

207
00:13:49,080 --> 00:13:50,200
Yanyan, come and eat.

208
00:13:50,399 --> 00:13:51,879
The food Mr. Gu ordered is delicious.

209
00:13:52,919 --> 00:13:54,039
He ordered this?

210
00:13:54,200 --> 00:13:54,840
Yes.

211
00:13:54,919 --> 00:13:57,600
But yours looks different from mine.

212
00:13:58,720 --> 00:14:00,759
Maybe Mr. Gu wanted to treat you,

213
00:14:00,840 --> 00:14:02,135
so he ordered food for the whole crew.

214
00:14:02,159 --> 00:14:03,000
No way.

215
00:14:03,080 --> 00:14:05,400
He probably ordered two kinds and handed
them out randomly.

216
00:14:11,399 --> 00:14:12,399
I'm too annoyed to eat.

217
00:14:14,639 --> 00:14:15,639
Hmph.

218
00:14:18,159 --> 00:14:19,159
Mr. Gu.

219
00:14:19,440 --> 00:14:20,440
How does it taste?

220
00:14:20,639 --> 00:14:21,639
I haven't tried it yet.

221
00:14:22,399 --> 00:14:23,440
Go on, eat.

222
00:14:34,279 --> 00:14:35,279
Mm.

223
00:14:35,360 --> 00:14:37,759
That's quite a special meal you ordered.

224
00:14:40,120 --> 00:14:41,240
I made it myself.

225
00:14:51,679 --> 00:14:53,239
Have you drunk from this bottle before?

226
00:14:54,080 --> 00:14:54,600
No.

227
00:14:54,840 --> 00:14:56,840
Chen brought it over. He said it was from
a fan.

228
00:14:57,799 --> 00:14:59,120
This bottle has been opened.

229
00:14:59,799 --> 00:15:02,240
Don't touch anything with a broken seal
from now on.

230
00:15:02,440 --> 00:15:05,120
Some fans put things in your food and
water.

231
00:15:06,200 --> 00:15:07,200
Got it.

232
00:15:08,120 --> 00:15:09,240
I'll get you another bottle.

233
00:15:10,039 --> 00:15:11,039
I swallowed it.

234
00:15:15,080 --> 00:15:16,360
Oh, wow! Wow!

235
00:15:16,399 --> 00:15:18,639
The Best Actor Top and His Pretty Bottom,
Part Two.

236
00:15:18,720 --> 00:15:19,720
A masterpiece.

237
00:15:20,159 --> 00:15:22,519
Let me appreciate this.

238
00:15:31,240 --> 00:15:32,960
Let me savor it.

239
00:15:40,799 --> 00:15:42,200
Why does this cushion

240
00:15:42,399 --> 00:15:43,759
feel less comfortable than before?

241
00:15:44,879 --> 00:15:48,519
Some stalker fans might put things in your
food and water.

242
00:16:05,759 --> 00:16:06,759
Huh?

243
00:16:08,039 --> 00:16:09,039
What the hell?

244
00:16:09,480 --> 00:16:11,080
Where's my two-thousand-yuan face cream?

245
00:16:13,799 --> 00:16:14,519
Hello, Yanyan?

246
00:16:14,600 --> 00:16:15,960
I brought your favorite milk tea.

247
00:16:17,080 --> 00:16:17,679
Mr. Gu.

248
00:16:17,879 --> 00:16:18,360
Done filming?

249
00:16:18,440 --> 00:16:19,440
Mm.

250
00:16:19,840 --> 00:16:21,840
I only brought one serving today.

251
00:16:23,879 --> 00:16:24,879
What?

252
00:16:25,440 --> 00:16:26,440
Something's missing?

253
00:16:26,759 --> 00:16:27,759
That doesn't seem likely.

254
00:16:28,559 --> 00:16:29,360
Don't panic.

255
00:16:29,399 --> 00:16:30,960
I'm in the parking lot right now.

256
00:16:31,320 --> 00:16:33,040
Ask reception to check the security
footage.

257
00:16:34,360 --> 00:16:34,919
Wei Yanzi,

258
00:16:35,120 --> 00:16:36,559
are you alone in your room?

259
00:16:38,799 --> 00:16:40,375
Make sure all the doors and windows are
shut.

260
00:16:40,399 --> 00:16:41,439
Lock the door from inside.

261
00:16:41,480 --> 00:16:42,520
I'm coming over right now.

262
00:16:42,559 --> 00:16:43,559
Okay?

263
00:16:44,279 --> 00:16:44,879
What's wrong?

264
00:16:45,039 --> 00:16:46,320
Yanyan's got a stalker fan.

265
00:16:46,559 --> 00:16:47,559
What?

266
00:16:48,039 --> 00:16:49,399
Come on! Hurry, hurry!

267
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:56,480
Yanyan!

268
00:16:56,559 --> 00:16:57,759
Stop filming! Stop filming!

269
00:16:57,879 --> 00:16:59,000
Stop filming! Stop filming!

270
00:16:59,360 --> 00:17:00,120
Stop filming!

271
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:01,240
Stop filming!

272
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:10,079
Mr. Gu, your key card.

273
00:17:24,559 --> 00:17:25,559
Mr. Gu.

274
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:27,000
Let's talk inside.

275
00:17:34,400 --> 00:17:35,200
Mr. Gu,

276
00:17:35,279 --> 00:17:36,376
it's really nothing serious.

277
00:17:36,400 --> 00:17:37,480
Sorry you had to rush over.

278
00:17:37,680 --> 00:17:38,680
Thank you.

279
00:17:38,720 --> 00:17:39,720
Between the two of us,

280
00:17:39,799 --> 00:17:40,879
there's no need for thanks.

281
00:17:46,039 --> 00:17:47,640
Go inside. Go inside.

282
00:17:50,200 --> 00:17:50,720
We've got a problem.

283
00:17:50,920 --> 00:17:52,255
A lot of stalker fans have shown up
downstairs.

284
00:17:52,279 --> 00:17:53,416
Security is trying to stop them,

285
00:17:53,440 --> 00:17:55,319
but a few may have got up the stairs.

286
00:17:55,480 --> 00:17:56,160
What?

287
00:17:56,319 --> 00:17:58,039
The hotel information must have been
leaked.

288
00:17:58,319 --> 00:17:58,839
Chen,

289
00:17:59,039 --> 00:18:00,559
ask the company to send more security.

290
00:18:00,640 --> 00:18:01,240
As soon as possible.

291
00:18:01,359 --> 00:18:02,359
Okay.

292
00:18:07,160 --> 00:18:08,480
If they got into your room,

293
00:18:08,720 --> 00:18:10,000
they must have your key card.

294
00:18:10,200 --> 00:18:11,440
It's not safe to stay here.

295
00:18:14,160 --> 00:18:15,160
Yanyan,

296
00:18:15,720 --> 00:18:16,720
do you trust me?

297
00:18:20,079 --> 00:18:21,279
Are you sure it's this floor?

298
00:18:21,519 --> 00:18:23,535
What did the person who sold you the
information say?

299
00:18:23,559 --> 00:18:26,119
He just said somewhere between floors
fifteen and twenty.

300
00:18:26,319 --> 00:18:27,839
For the exact room number,

301
00:18:27,920 --> 00:18:29,095
I'd have to pay another thirty thousand
yuan.

302
00:18:29,119 --> 00:18:30,480
Thirty thousand?

303
00:18:30,680 --> 00:18:32,280
That wouldn't even cover a photo for me.

304
00:18:32,640 --> 00:18:34,400
Forget it. Let's just stake it out
ourselves.

305
00:18:34,920 --> 00:18:36,839
We might even catch Gu Yiliang.

306
00:18:37,079 --> 00:18:37,960
I don't ship those two.

307
00:18:38,039 --> 00:18:40,119
Two straight guys faking it. It's forced
and cringey.

308
00:18:41,480 --> 00:18:42,480
Not this way.

309
00:18:43,119 --> 00:18:45,160
You say that, but you still came with me.

310
00:18:49,759 --> 00:18:51,119
Good thing you reacted so quickly.

311
00:18:51,880 --> 00:18:53,240
We can't stay here forever.

312
00:18:53,480 --> 00:18:54,520
Let's head upstairs first.

313
00:19:08,559 --> 00:19:09,559
I can't.

314
00:19:09,599 --> 00:19:10,599
I'm exhausted.

315
00:19:10,839 --> 00:19:11,839
I need to sit down.

316
00:19:12,160 --> 00:19:13,160
Otherwise,

317
00:19:13,200 --> 00:19:15,000
I'll need a wheelchair to get to set
tomorrow.

318
00:19:16,119 --> 00:19:17,839
I could carry you to work on my back.

319
00:19:19,599 --> 00:19:20,680
Sounds lovely.

320
00:19:21,279 --> 00:19:23,839
Remember that livestream when you stood in
the center by mistake?

321
00:19:24,079 --> 00:19:26,119
They said you disrespected the senior
actor there.

322
00:19:26,279 --> 00:19:27,000
That day,

323
00:19:27,200 --> 00:19:30,079
I was offering incense at Nanpu Temple,
two thousand kilometers away.

324
00:19:30,279 --> 00:19:31,640
Some haters took photos of me

325
00:19:31,799 --> 00:19:34,559
and said I was casting a curse on you from
afar.

326
00:19:35,319 --> 00:19:36,319
So, my rival,

327
00:19:36,759 --> 00:19:38,519
if anything really happens to me,

328
00:19:39,160 --> 00:19:40,759
you'll be the prime suspect.

329
00:19:41,640 --> 00:19:43,400
So we've been inseparable

330
00:19:44,599 --> 00:19:45,640
since way back then.

331
00:19:47,518 --> 00:19:50,713
So this is where the sweet stuff is!

332
00:19:57,799 --> 00:19:59,680
Oh, I'm not cold.

333
00:20:01,160 --> 00:20:02,360
I'm hot from all that running.

334
00:20:05,079 --> 00:20:09,112
How are you so good at giving shippers sweet
moments? How are your romantic moves so advanced?

335
00:20:21,086 --> 00:20:25,965
The fanfics really had it right. At a time
like this, a third wheel is bound to show up.

336
00:20:31,039 --> 00:20:32,039
Hello?

337
00:20:32,839 --> 00:20:33,839
Got it.

338
00:20:34,039 --> 00:20:34,599
Okay.

339
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:35,960
Bye.

340
00:20:40,319 --> 00:20:41,639
Chen just told me

341
00:20:41,640 --> 00:20:44,055
the stalker who stole my key card was
taken away by the police.

342
00:20:44,079 --> 00:20:45,920
The others have all been sent away too.

343
00:20:46,400 --> 00:20:48,880
The hotel manager and the security team
Mr. Cheng hired

344
00:20:49,079 --> 00:20:51,480
will thoroughly check the hotel tonight.

345
00:20:52,440 --> 00:20:54,200
You should still stay somewhere else
tonight.

346
00:20:54,480 --> 00:20:56,320
It's hard to find a place at this hour,
though.

347
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,920
And there's the privacy issue.

348
00:20:59,079 --> 00:21:00,440
You've got a point.

349
00:21:01,680 --> 00:21:02,799
Then how about your place?

350
00:21:03,039 --> 00:21:04,599
I could see the cat too.

351
00:21:09,640 --> 00:21:11,960
Unless it's inconvenient.

352
00:21:13,039 --> 00:21:14,039
Sure.

353
00:21:14,079 --> 00:21:15,079
It's fine.

354
00:21:16,000 --> 00:21:17,000
To see the cat.

355
00:21:17,240 --> 00:21:17,720
Okay.

356
00:21:17,759 --> 00:21:19,000
I'll let Chen know.

357
00:21:21,119 --> 00:21:22,119
To see the cat.

358
00:21:26,000 --> 00:21:27,000
Understood.

359
00:21:27,279 --> 00:21:29,759
Have the hotel move them to another floor
after the inspection.

360
00:21:29,960 --> 00:21:31,000
And arrange more security.

361
00:21:44,160 --> 00:21:45,400
Oh, Lucas.

362
00:21:45,759 --> 00:21:46,759
Why are you still here?

363
00:21:47,640 --> 00:21:49,200
I'm waiting for my night scene.

364
00:21:50,920 --> 00:21:51,960
That scene was cut.

365
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:54,480
They must have forgotten to tell you.

366
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:57,480
I see. Thank you.

367
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:58,880
No problem. It's getting late.

368
00:21:58,920 --> 00:21:59,799
You should head back soon.

369
00:21:59,799 --> 00:22:00,079
Okay.

370
00:22:00,080 --> 00:22:01,255
It's hard to get a cab this late.

371
00:22:01,279 --> 00:22:02,079
I'm heading off. Bye.

372
00:22:02,119 --> 00:22:03,119
Okay.

373
00:22:13,039 --> 00:22:14,039
Mingming.

374
00:22:20,119 --> 00:22:22,240
Why isn't he saying anything?

375
00:22:24,493 --> 00:22:27,759
Quiet. So quiet. Way too quiet.

376
00:22:28,000 --> 00:22:29,136
Even my veins aren't this still.

377
00:22:29,160 --> 00:22:30,440
Even Shizuka isn't this quiet.

378
00:22:30,599 --> 00:22:32,136
Even Jingtai District isn't this quiet.

379
00:22:32,160 --> 00:22:34,480
Even calming tonic isn't this calming.

380
00:22:35,079 --> 00:22:36,759
How about some music?

381
00:22:39,440 --> 00:22:43,585
I love you, my dear Gu Yiliang.

382
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:47,720
Silence is nice, actually.

383
00:22:49,579 --> 00:22:53,266
It's been so long. Why
hasn't he said anything?

384
00:22:53,558 --> 00:22:56,759
Why does he still look
so nervous?

385
00:22:59,680 --> 00:23:01,279
Why do I feel like

386
00:23:01,359 --> 00:23:03,440
we keep going in circles?

387
00:23:05,720 --> 00:23:07,240
I need to get some things for home.

388
00:23:07,920 --> 00:23:09,400
I'm looking for somewhere on the way.

389
00:23:12,440 --> 00:23:13,000
A supermarket.

390
00:23:13,279 --> 00:23:14,279
A supermarket?

391
00:23:15,240 --> 00:23:16,519
There's one just ahead.

392
00:23:16,640 --> 00:23:18,519
We've already passed it three times.

393
00:23:28,799 --> 00:23:30,559
I'll get it. Wait in the car.

394
00:23:38,480 --> 00:23:41,440
What is he buying? He's acting so strange.

395
00:24:01,920 --> 00:24:03,039
Yes, that's just right.

396
00:24:09,279 --> 00:24:10,279
Watch where you're going.

397
00:24:18,680 --> 00:24:20,599
Take me with you when you eat from now on.

398
00:24:20,880 --> 00:24:22,320
I'll help you finish the other half.

399
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:23,880
Sure.

400
00:24:25,640 --> 00:24:26,640
What did you say?

401
00:24:27,240 --> 00:24:28,240
I didn't catch that.

402
00:24:29,680 --> 00:24:31,319
It looks like you've got heat rash.

403
00:24:31,519 --> 00:24:32,839
I brought you some talcum powder.

404
00:24:33,359 --> 00:24:34,679
You don't have to force yourself.

405
00:24:35,160 --> 00:24:36,160
I'm not.

406
00:24:36,786 --> 00:24:37,786
It's settled, then.

407
00:24:39,079 --> 00:24:40,159
I'll come over from now on.

408
00:24:40,479 --> 00:24:41,479
Come to my place.

409
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,720
It's safer here.

410
00:24:47,519 --> 00:24:48,519
So, my rival,

411
00:24:49,693 --> 00:24:51,372
why are you so protective of me?

412
00:24:53,946 --> 00:24:55,146
I'd like to ask you that too.

413
00:24:55,706 --> 00:24:57,186
Why am I so protective of you?

414
00:24:57,680 --> 00:24:58,680
Hey, rival.

415
00:25:02,326 --> 00:25:05,406
[What should happen will happen, what
should make you feel will make you feel]

416
00:25:41,160 --> 00:25:42,160
Got everything?

417
00:25:45,599 --> 00:25:48,279
That's all? Why was he so nervous, then?

418
00:25:51,079 --> 00:25:52,079
Let's go.

419
00:25:58,319 --> 00:26:00,359
Continue straight ahead.

420
00:26:05,680 --> 00:26:07,359
What's going on?

421
00:26:07,440 --> 00:26:09,640
Why isn't Gu Yiliang nervous anymore,

422
00:26:09,720 --> 00:26:11,720
but now I am?

423
00:26:16,520 --> 00:26:18,720
What exactly is he planning?

424
00:26:18,799 --> 00:26:20,559
This isn't the road home.

425
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:24,758
This is clearly the road to... to...

426
00:26:32,240 --> 00:26:34,680
Follow the bend ahead.

427
00:26:51,799 --> 00:26:52,799
Come in.

428
00:26:53,720 --> 00:26:56,372
Have I... gone gay?

429
00:26:57,960 --> 00:26:58,960
Come on in.

430
00:26:59,559 --> 00:27:00,559
Oh.

431
00:27:01,920 --> 00:27:02,720
Have a seat.

432
00:27:02,839 --> 00:27:03,960
I'll get some fruit.

433
00:27:04,279 --> 00:27:05,279
Ah.

434
00:27:12,200 --> 00:27:13,480
No way. No way.

435
00:27:13,519 --> 00:27:15,000
I'm a straight man.

436
00:27:19,680 --> 00:27:21,119
"Give Me the Time of a Song,"

437
00:27:21,200 --> 00:27:24,119
some invisible hands have dragged me out
of the closet.

438
00:27:24,200 --> 00:27:26,640
No way. Absolutely not.

439
00:27:37,640 --> 00:27:39,696
Am I crazy? Why am I already
assuming I'm the bottom?

440
00:27:39,720 --> 00:27:40,960
If anything, I'd be the top.

441
00:27:43,559 --> 00:27:45,160
Wait, why am I assuming I'm gay at all?

442
00:27:45,240 --> 00:27:46,519
Wei Yanzi, calm down.

443
00:27:46,599 --> 00:27:49,039
I can't lose my head at a time like this.

444
00:28:12,319 --> 00:28:13,319
Gu Yiliang.

445
00:28:14,599 --> 00:28:16,240
My rival has made his feelings clear.

446
00:28:18,920 --> 00:28:20,039
I can't back down now.

447
00:28:25,130 --> 00:28:26,610
[Bonus Content: Gu Yiliang's Diary 2]

448
00:28:26,880 --> 00:28:29,039
Douya, make a note of this.

449
00:28:30,039 --> 00:28:31,559
Today, my rival told me...

450
00:28:33,880 --> 00:28:35,039
I'm already great as I am.

451
00:28:35,519 --> 00:28:36,519
Oh my God.

452
00:28:36,542 --> 00:28:39,857
Hearing a rival say you're great
as you are is really affecting.

453
00:28:40,099 --> 00:28:43,379
That recognition means even
more than becoming friends.

454
00:28:43,640 --> 00:28:45,559
And yet I've become his sugar daddy.

455
00:28:46,759 --> 00:28:48,159
In my three years in this industry,

456
00:28:48,799 --> 00:28:52,079
I've done all I can to avoid
its shady arrangements.

457
00:28:53,000 --> 00:28:54,079
I never imagined...

458
00:28:55,279 --> 00:28:56,720
I'd end up keeping someone myself.

459
00:28:58,079 --> 00:28:59,279
My sincere advice:

460
00:28:59,720 --> 00:29:02,799
end this transactional
relationship as soon as possible.

461
00:29:02,920 --> 00:29:04,039
Maintain your integrity.

462
00:29:05,079 --> 00:29:06,079
Impossible.

463
00:29:06,759 --> 00:29:09,200
This wasn't an impulsive decision.

464
00:29:09,599 --> 00:29:11,960
I carefully thought it
over for three cigarettes.

465
00:29:14,160 --> 00:29:15,160
During the first,

466
00:29:17,599 --> 00:29:18,720
I really did hesitate.

467
00:29:19,160 --> 00:29:22,640
But my rival looked at me with such trust

468
00:29:23,079 --> 00:29:24,480
that I simply couldn't reject

469
00:29:24,880 --> 00:29:26,559
the trust he placed in me.

470
00:29:31,000 --> 00:29:32,039
During the second,

471
00:29:33,480 --> 00:29:37,079
I assessed my finances and connections.

472
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:39,079
I thought.

473
00:29:39,720 --> 00:29:41,080
I could give him something better.

474
00:29:42,279 --> 00:29:43,319
No question about that.

475
00:29:45,640 --> 00:29:46,640
During the third,

476
00:29:47,599 --> 00:29:48,720
I considered

477
00:29:50,480 --> 00:29:51,960
what would happen to our relationship

478
00:29:52,160 --> 00:29:55,680
if it were discovered and exposed.

479
00:29:57,359 --> 00:29:58,799
Actually, nothing much would happen.

480
00:30:00,440 --> 00:30:03,359
We could pass it off as promoting our
on-screen pairing.

481
00:30:04,200 --> 00:30:05,279
If we really got exposed,

482
00:30:05,880 --> 00:30:07,560
we'd cross that bridge when we came to it.

483
00:30:08,079 --> 00:30:09,079
Right?

484
00:30:09,440 --> 00:30:13,920
Conclusion: improper
smoking leads to moral decline.

485
00:30:17,240 --> 00:30:19,480
I'm supposed to be his sugar daddy,

486
00:30:20,319 --> 00:30:23,358
but he won't take the
opportunities I offer, or my gifts.

487
00:30:23,599 --> 00:30:26,039
He even insists on splitting the
assistant's salary evenly.

488
00:30:29,880 --> 00:30:31,319
Today, he even said...

489
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:34,839
I'm already great as I am.

490
00:30:37,519 --> 00:30:38,519
Tell me,

491
00:30:39,599 --> 00:30:40,880
should I kiss him?

492
00:30:43,920 --> 00:30:46,480
Would you like me to use your search
history

493
00:30:46,559 --> 00:30:49,680
to recommend some new fanfic collections?

494
00:30:51,559 --> 00:30:52,559
No.
